{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfr9SFcWXugHcWpT5kZ58","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Outcome: queue with five edges.** Nothing in the cluster contradicts the spine, none of it was already done, and no two rows are one work item. Five pairs could be claimed side by side and fight over the same code, so each gets a hard `needs` edge.\n\nThe commit is `aca5bb9e` on `wi-875` and carries the `WI: WI-875` trailer. The pre-commit checks ended `RESULT: PASS`. It holds the verdict (`docs/reviews/wi-875-adjudicate-queue-overlap-4214/001-ADJUDICATE-6fe2f8b.md`) and the `## Consolidation` block added to WI-875's spec. I didn't commit the `.requested` binding file, because the route records it in its own telemetry commit, so it is still untracked.\n\n**Starting point.** The three WI-855 sittings had already judged 26 of these 30 rows, and their edges are in the files. I didn't reopen those rulings. This sitting judged:\n- the four new rows, WI-856 to WI-859;\n- the pairs that became claimable together now that WI-846, WI-849, WI-852, WI-860 and WI-865 have landed.\n\n**The edges** (the row that waits, then the row it waits on):\n\n| Waits | On | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| WI-858 | WI-847 | WI-834, WI-847 and WI-858 all change the retained session's lease and retirement code and amend LLR-270. WI-858 is claimable today with nothing ordering it. With this edge the order is WI-834, then WI-847, then WI-858. |\n| WI-800 | WI-858 | WI-800 replaces the store that WI-858 changes, so the new store has to carry WI-858's contention fix. |\n| WI-809 | WI-857 | Both add the same check to WI-849's approval rung: the session that judged an act must not have authored its rows. WI-809 already says \"no second actor test\", so it builds on WI-857's session records. |\n| WI-810 | WI-856 | WI-810 folds the consolidation close into the mint step, so it should carry WI-856's change to `edged_text`. |\n| WI-811 | WI-853 | WI-811 extends WI-853's findings gate. Its only route to WI-853 went through WI-805, and the owner dropped that edge on 2026-10-08. |\n\n**Checked and ruled out:**\n- **Not already done:** WI-866 didn't fix what WI-856 asks for: `edged_text` still returns None for a row with no `needs` line (`consolidate.py:1425`). WI-859's test still treats the last line of output as pytest's summary (`test_conftest_isolation.py:52`).\n- **Not a spine conflict:** WI-858's lockless marker doesn't break SR-227's \"one writer at a time\" rule. The record is still written whole under the lock, and the marker works like the tombstone files LLR-270 already describes.\n- **Not merged:** I didn't fold WI-857 into WI-809. The owner deliberately made WI-857 its own row, and WI-809 is already the largest slice of the design.\n\n**For WI-848's builder (no edge needed):** its Done-when describes the interim dispute procedure \"until WI-865 lands\", and WI-865 has now landed. Its existing bullet about reconciling with every landed row already covers this, so the skill should describe the landed dispute path.\n\nAll five waiting rows already have a `needs` line, so the machinery can write every edge without refusing the verdict."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":299,"cache_read_input_tokens":174934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":299},"output_tokens":797,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41fe7d99-acbe-4bcf-919b-66cec7cec473","uuid":"3a97976e-45a6-40be-9be8-a671c85c3319","timestamp":"2026-10-09T05:55:19.669Z","request_id":"req_011Cfr9SFFSNjcet7Exyemtg"}
